TurboScript serial examples
===========================

These examples use the public TurboSerial ABI from `turbo_serial.h`.
They do not include `libserialport.h` or call `sp_*` APIs directly.

Examples
--------

- `list_ports.c` - creates a port-list snapshot and prints visible port names.
- `port_info.c` - reads metadata for one named port.
- `port_config.c` - configures and opens one serial handle.
- `send_receive.c` - performs blocking write/read on one open handle.
- `await_events.c` - waits for readiness through a TurboSerial event set.
- `handle_errors.c` - handles `turbo_serial_result_t` at the application boundary.

Build
-----

Examples are not part of the default build because most need real serial
hardware or a configured virtual port to run. They can be compiled from the
repository root with:

```text
cmake --build build/Msvc --target turbo_serial_examples --config Debug
```

Run a specific example with the port name used by the current system:

```text
build/Msvc/bin/example_port_info.exe COM1
```

Validation
----------

The examples are compile-checked through the `turbo_serial_examples` target.
The public ABI itself is covered by:

```text
ctest --test-dir build/Msvc -C Debug -R test_turbo_serial_public_abi --output-on-failure
```
